6】【BP855】\n\n## Integrations and development\n\nIntegration documentation explains finding, installing, configuring, and using Hub integrations, developing custom integrations with the CLI, SDK, and HTTP Client, and working with actions, events, channels, handlers, schemas, configuration, logging, and secrets. 【BP036】【BP189】【BP266】【BP459】【BP522】【BP531】【BP747】\n\nChannel and service guides cover Zendesk, Zapier, WhatsApp, Webhooks, Vonage, Viber, Trello, Slack, Telegram, Twilio, Sunshine Conversations, Notion, LINE, Messenger, Microsoft Teams, Intercom, Instagram, and Asana. They address setup and credentials, messaging, triggers and actions, webhooks, testing, and—in applicable cases—human handoff or platform-specific constraints. 【BP009】【BP018】【BP045】【BP054】【BP180】【BP198】【BP234】【BP243】【BP261】【BP270】【BP279】【BP360】【BP387】【BP396】【BP405】【BP477】【BP540】【BP900】\n\nDeveloper resources include the CLI, SDK bot and integration definitions, message and event handlers, scheduled events, the Chat API, and custom LLM integrations. 【BP351】【BP783】【BP801】【BP450】\n\n## Webchat, APIs, and data\n\nWebchat documentation covers native deployment, embed code, shareable links, styling, configuration, domain whitelisting, user data, widget controls, events, browser messaging, and React components. Platform-specific embedding guides cover Wix, Webflow, and WordPress. Webchat v1 is deprecated as the platform transitions to v2; v2 resources include CSS, React components, and the client. 【BP090】【BP126】【BP027】【BP072】【BP099】【BP063】【BP081】【BP144】【BP267】【BP315】【BP402】【BP720】【BP765】\n\nFiles and Chat APIs support bot messaging and file operations, including upload, download, search, metadata, permissions, and semantic indexing. Conversation tools cover raw histories, summaries, transcripts, dashboard inspection, and exporting or paginating messages. 【BP140】【BP142】【BP576】【BP585】【BP612】【BP702】\n\nBot archives support import and export, with guidance on included content and warnings about overwriting bots and reconfiguring integrations. Analytics documentation covers dashboards, charts, event tracking, API exports, and streaming behavioral data to external services. 【BP486】【BP225】【BP729】【BP738】【BP909】\n\n## Testing, monitoring, and safety\n\nTesting and troubleshooting resources include the Emulator, Event Debugger, execution and production logs, event payloads, resource monitoring, and issue inspection. 【BP432】【BP441】【BP504】【BP675】【BP693】\n\nSafety guidance covers AI guardrails, access control, privacy, monitoring, fallback and human escalation, abuse prevention, rate limits, spending limits, and review of retrieved data and decision logic. HITL resources document escalation, review gates, live-agent participation, and custom integration support. 【BP306】【BP369】【BP567】【BP639】【BP837】"","role":"user"}],"model":"openai:gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18","responseFormat":"json","temperature":0},"method":"POST","url":"https://api.botpress.cloud/v2/cognitive/generate-text"}

